    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36868" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαπόλλῡμι </span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαπλ-ύων</span></b>  prob. cj. in <i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Ch.</u>
			837
		</span></i> (lyr.)), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>destroy
				utterly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				588
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				950
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				8.7.2
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, with pf.
			<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαπόλωλα</span>: aor. 2
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαπωλόμην</span>:—<i>perish
				utterly out of,</i> c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλίον ἐξαπολοίατ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.60
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαπόλωλε δόμων κειμήλια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.290
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠέλιος δὲ οὐρανοῦ ἐξαπόλωλε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					20.357
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπέρμα πάσης ἐξαπόλλυται χθονός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					528
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>perish utterly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.173
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				236
			</span></i>.</div>
